// Go SDK (`pkg/sdk`) lets an embedding program do with a client, a session or
// the long-term memory is reachable from here, so a client in another language
// (the Python package in `python/`) gets the same surface as a Go host.
//
// The engine stays in Go: this contract is served by `cmd/grpc`, which adapts
// `pkg/sdk` to these messages. Nothing is reimplemented on the client side, so
// a Python caller runs the exact same tool loop, providers, permissions and
// persistence as the terminal interface.
//
// Three services:
//
//   SeshatService   server-wide: health, models, skills, MCP servers, sessions
//   SessionService  one conversation: turns, events, approvals, tools, plans
//   MemoryService   long-term memory graph
//   WorkflowService workflows (validate, draft, run)
//
// Streaming. A turn is driven by `SessionService.SubmitMessageStream`, which
// returns `SessionEvent` messages for the whole turn and ends with
// `TurnCompleted` (carrying the full `TurnResult`) or `TurnFailed`. The same
// events are available for any session through `SessionService.Subscribe`, so a
// UI can attach to a turn another call started, and can resume after a
// reconnection by replaying from `from_sequence`.
//
